+## Previous feature bundle — 2026-09-28 (D-349)
+
+**Stop Token Movement supports bounded multi-token cached preplanning.** For a group movement, the host can plan one eligible Stop-bearing Enter/Exit graph per moved token in deterministic order. Each exact outcome—including conditions, gates and RNG—is cached and reused by post-commit dispatch; planning later tokens against the staged fork preserves earlier history for gate evaluation. The movement envelope shares the preflight timestamp with graph history, but graph operations remain separate commits. A token is clipped only if Stop ran and the plan is restricted to root graph history plus that token's position/flags.
+
+**Boundaries:** limited to at most 128 moving tokens, 4096 graph definitions and 65,536 token/definition checks; one scene and at most one crossing candidate per token. Competing/ambiguous shapes and graphs with `move`, `rotate`, `triggerTile`, `sequence`, `script`, `summon` or `resetHistory` fall back to post-commit behavior. Root graph variable changes and other side effects keep movement and graph commits separate. In-flight canvas animation and waypoint paths are still not interrupted.
+
+Executed: **4590 unit passes / 12 skips**, 321 passing files/two skipped; full run **139.45 s**. Host sync + core automation files **259 passed**. Typecheck, lint, production preparation, size and whitespace passed; bundle **3,938,455 raw / 1,126,185 gzip bytes**. Production Chromium movement regression passed **7/7 in 6.3 min**, including two-token conditional Stop intent via the host GM client. Full details: [FX_WIZARD_VERIFICATION_HISTORY.md](FX_WIZARD_VERIFICATION_HISTORY.md#report-d349).
+
+**Still partial:** unsupported, ambiguous, multi-scene and multiple-crossing cases use ordinary post-commit behavior; no active drag/animation or waypoint interruption. Cross-browser/performance/A01–A41, environment/scheduler, attachments, audio/template authoring and full parity remain incomplete.
