n the four shapes and theirs on it; and resolution: 8 units → 160 px through the scene metric with `scaleTo` travelling as the author's ratio), 3 in `tests/canvas/fxStyle.test.ts` (the drawn polygon is its own vertices and bounds and says nothing about facing, its cutout hides what is inside, and its ratio/turn read out of the polygon) and 1 host case in `tests/host/sync.test.ts` (a drawn region reaching the cue as offsets with `animate.scale`, 8 forged regions never reaching the store, the unwalled U accepted) — plus the `fx_sequence` drawn-region phase (that spec's chromium run is in the gates below); before that, +8 cases for D-314 — 2 in `tests/core/fx.test.ts` (the per-shape cross-axis field lists, their own bounds and the wall refusal; the resolved ratio/frame/`fan` for a rect and a cone, the absent-spread default and `scale` surviving beside a pinned cross axis), 5 in `tests/canvas/fxStyle.test.ts` (the ratio walking from the authored shape, restarting per cycle, with the frame in radians; a widened ray exactly wider at the same reach; a growth beside a pinned width landing each axis on its own number versus D-305's uniform growth; a cone's edge vertex swinging to the doubled half-angle at the same radius while the stretch path fattens the arc instead; a turn composing with a width in the shape's own frame) and 1 host case in `tests/host/sync.test.ts` (a beam that thickens reaching the cue as `{scale, cross: {ratio, axisDeg}}`, with 5 forged cross axes never reaching the store)); before that, +8 cases for D-313 — 3 in `tests/core/fx.test.ts` (the 2–4 bound, the both-spellings and per-entry range refusals, the canonical read/write round-trip that stores the shorthand when a chain is trimmed to one, the ordered plan and the per-frame per-entry walk), 4 in `tests/canvas/fxStyle.test.ts` (authored order with one instance per entry, an animated entry nudging only itself, two entries animating on their own ends, the shorthand rendering as the same one-entry look) a